FILED s542r (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-16, the round on main code cc36604b = MAIN-READY-95) from the companion: t/run/switches.t 125/15 (the snapshot) -> 118/13, rows 132-140 ("-E enables 'say' feature" .. "-X with use 5.36") never produced; the file's top-level form aborts at t-line 680 with "Not a GLOB reference" (PCL recovery line in the kept output, ~/pcl-agent-scratch/s542/round/comp1/main/keep/run_switches.t.out).

REPRO (scratch/s542r/probes/reopendir.pl in the s542r worktree):

    use strict; use warnings;
    my $dir = "/tmp";
    opendir my $d, $dir or die "first opendir: $!";
    my @n = readdir $d;
    closedir $d;
    print "first: ", (@n ? "read" : "none"), "\n";
    opendir $d, $dir or die "second opendir: $!";     # PCL dies here: Not a GLOB reference
    my @m = readdir $d;
    closedir $d;
    print "second: ", (@m ? "read" : "none"), "\n";
    print "ref after: ", ref(\$d), " ", (ref $d), "\n";

perl 5.40.3: first: read / second: read / ref after: REF GLOB
PCL main (cc36604b) and MR-91: first: read, then dies "Not a GLOB reference" (a raw top-level abort, rc 255).
PCL MR-86 .. MR-90: first: read / second: read / ref after: SCALAR ARRAY  (the re-open worked; `ref $d` was already wrong).

BISECT (one probe per merge tree, ~/pcl-agent-scratch/s542/round/specs/probe-reopendir.log; the companion file itself: MR-85 125/15, MR-91 118/13, comp1/leg.log): MR-90 938cc88d works, MR-91 3246e41a (s538a) dies -- s538a's #3618: %p-fh-place-check (every opener's install slot) asks %p-stat-handle-shaped-p whether the variable already holds a handle-shaped value, and dies "Not a GLOB reference" otherwise, as perl's rv2gv does for \$code / [1] / {}.  PCL's DIRHANDLE value in a lexical is not a GLOB reference (`ref $d` answers ARRAY where perl answers GLOB), so the predicate calls it a non-handle and the second opendir dies.

TWO DEFECTS, ONE CAUSE: (1) the regression -- an opener's place check must accept a dirhandle (the predicate must know the dirhandle representation; rule 11: the one handle-designator predicate, not a second copy); (2) pre-existing -- `opendir my $d` should leave a GLOB reference in $d (ref $d eq 'GLOB', ref \$d eq 'REF'), which would make (1) a non-issue.  Probe also `opendir` after `close`-of-a-file-handle variable, `open $d` on a variable that held a dirhandle, and a bareword DIRHANDLE re-opened.

BASELINE: the seven run/switches.t rows 132-136 139 140 are keyed #5082 in baselines/perl-suite-fails.tsv and the file's row-shortfall row 0 -> 9 (s542r); the snapshot row is edited to 118/13 with this cause.  CLOSE-WITH-ROWS: those rows leave with the fix.
